d, crew cheering raggedly.\n\nThrough the fire they saw it: Pirate Queen Vex's flagship, waiting in the storm's eye like a spider. 'They knew the route,' Commander Sera Ilsa said. 'Someone sold the starlog.' The betrayal sat cold in their stomach."}, {'n': 4, 'title': "The Traitor's Price", 'text': "The traitor showed themselves at the third waypoint: the signal officer, paid in promises by Pirate Queen Vex. They seized a distress beacon and ran for the escape pod with Pirate Queen Vex's ships closing in.\n\nCommander Sera Ilsa laughed for the first time in days. 'All this way,' they said, 'and we were carrying the lock, not the treasure.' Navigator Bo Tak was already calculating the wake-up sequence.\n\nNavigator Bo Tak caught them at the airlock. There was no fight — only the traitor crying that Pirate Queen Vex held their family. Commander Sera Ilsa understood, and hated understanding. Mercy, out here, was a luxury with teeth."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Grid Awakens', 'text': "The duel was legend before it ended: two ships in the fire-light, neither yielding, until Commander Sera Ilsa did the impossible — dove through the grid's own gate, which a distress beacon held open, and watched Pirate Queen Vex break against the shield they could not see.\n\nNavigator Bo Tak fed a distress beacon into the ancient console. For a heartbeat nothing happened — then the sky caught fire, a lattice of light wrapping the Shattered Belt like a held breath. Pirate Queen Vex's vanguard shattered against it like waves on rock.\n\nSilence, then. The grid humming. the Shattered Belt safe below. Navigator Bo Tak put a hand on Commander Sera Ilsa's shoulder and said what everyone was thinking: 'We live.'"}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Home Signal', 'text': "Commander Sera Ilsa stood on the hull at sunset, watching the Shattered Belt turn below. courage among the stars — the stars had taught it, and the crew had proved it, and the grid would remember it.\n\nNavigator Bo Tak was offered an admiralty 